content.reasoning:
The body_preview already shows me what I need. Let me extract from the preview:

```json
{
  "resources": {
    "vehicle_positions": {
      "canonical": "/v3/positions",
      "deprecated_aliases": ["/v1/locations", "/v2/pings"]
    },
    "trip_history": {
      "canonical": "/v3/trips",
      "deprecated_aliases": ["/v1/journeys"],
      "not": "/v2/routes (planned routes)"
    },
    "sensor_frames": {
      "canonical": "/v3/sensor-frames",
      "deprecated_aliases": ["/v2/sensors"]
    },
    "geofence_events": {
      "canonical": "/v3/geofence-events",
      "not": "/v3/geofences (definitions)"
    }
  }
}
```

So for `geofence_events`:
- `canonical_path`: `/v3/geofence-events`
- `not_path`: `/v3/geofences (definitions)`

The user wants the `not_path` exactly as the catalog flags it — so the full string including the parenthetical. Let me report.
